{"id":"mahabharata-13-015","work":"mahabharata","part":13,"partName":"अनुशासनपर्व","partNameEn":"Anushasana Parva","unit":15,"title":"पञ्चदशोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 15 · Krishna's worship of Shiva","summary":{"en":"Upamanyu tells Krishna how Shiva would never withhold grace from one who thinks of him as Krishna has. Krishna, after the long penance, sees the god with Uma, and Shiva offers him eight boons.","kn":"ಕೃಷ್ಣನಂತೆ ಧ್ಯಾನಿಸಿದವನಿಗೆ ಶಿವ ಕೃಪೆ ತಡೆಯುವುದಿಲ್ಲವೆಂದು ಉಪಮನ್ಯು ಕೃಷ್ಣನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ದೀರ್ಘ ತಪಸ್ಸಿನ ನಂತರ ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಉಮೆಯೊಡನೆ ದೇವನನ್ನು ಕಾಣುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಶಿವ ಎಂಟು ವರಗಳನ್ನು ನೀಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"उपमन्यु कृष्ण से कहते हैं कि जो कृष्ण की तरह शिव का ध्यान करे उससे शिव कभी कृपा नहीं रोकते। लम्बे तप के बाद कृष्ण उमा सहित देव को देखते हैं और शिव उन्हें आठ वर देते हैं।","te":"కృష్ణునిలా ధ్యానించినవానికి శివుడు కృప ఎప్పుడూ ఆపడని ఉపమన్యుడు కృష్ణునికి చెబుతాడు. దీర్ఘ తపస్సు తరువాత కృష్ణుడు ఉమతో దేవుని చూస్తాడు, శివుడు ఎనిమిది వరాలు ఇస్తాడు.","ta":"கிருஷ்ணனைப் போல் தியானித்தவருக்கு சிவன் அருளைத் தடுக்கமாட்டார் என்று உபமன்யு கிருஷ்ணனிடம் கூறுகிறார். நீண்ட தவத்துக்குப் பின் கிருஷ்ணன் உமையுடன் இறைவனைக் காண்கிறார், சிவன் எட்டு வரங்கள் அளிக்கிறார்.","ml":"കൃഷ്ണൻ ചെയ്യുന്നതുപോലെ തന്നെ ധ്യാനിക്കുന്നവന് ശിവൻ ഒരിക്കലും കൃപ നിഷേധിക്കില്ലെന്ന് ഉപമന്യു കൃഷ്ണനോട് പറയുന്നു. ദീർഘമായ തപസ്സിനുശേഷം ഉമയോടൊപ്പമുള്ള ദേവനെ കൃഷ്ണൻ കാണുന്നു; ശിവൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തിന് എട്ടു വരങ്ങൾ നൽകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 13.15; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Nov 03 2026","sections":[{"title":"आनुशासनिकपर्व","titleEn":"Anushasanika Parva (The instructions)","verses":[{"text":"उपमन्युरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Upamanyu said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एतान्सहस्रशश्चान्यान्समनुध्यातवान्हरः ।\nकस्मात्प्रसादं भगवान्न कुर्यात्तव माधव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hara has contemplated these and thousands of others; why, Madhava, would the blessed lord not show you favor?"}},{"n":2,"text":"त्वादृशेन हि देवानां श्लाघनीयः समागमः ।\nब्रह्मण्येनानृशंसेन श्रद्दधानेन चाप्युत ।\nजप्यं च ते प्रदास्यामि येन द्रक्ष्यसि शंकरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For one like you, a meeting with the gods is praiseworthy, for you are devoted to brahmins, compassionate and full of faith. I will give you a mantra to recite, by which you will see Shankara."}},{"text":"कृष्ण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Krishna said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"अब्रुवं तमहं ब्रह्मंस्त्वत्प्रसादान्महामुने ।\nद्रक्ष्ये दितिजसंघानां मर्दनं त्रिदशेश्वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I said to him, \"Brahmin, great sage, by your grace I shall see the lord of the gods, the crusher of the hosts of Diti's sons.\""}},{"n":4,"text":"दिनेऽष्टमे च विप्रेण दीक्षितोऽहं यथाविधि ।\nदण्डी मुण्डी कुशी चीरी घृताक्तो मेखली तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"On the eighth day I was initiated by the brahmin according to rule: carrying a staff, shaven-headed, with kusha grass, in bark garments, smeared with ghee and girdled."}},{"n":5,"text":"मासमेकं फलाहारो द्वितीयं सलिलाशनः ।\nतृतीयं च चतुर्थं च पञ्चमं चानिलाशनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For one month I lived on fruit, the second on water, and the third and fourth and fifth on air."}},{"n":6,"text":"एकपादेन तिष्ठंश्च ऊर्ध्वबाहुरतन्द्रितः ।\nतेजः सूर्यसहस्रस्य अपश्यं दिवि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Standing on one foot with arms raised, unwearied, I saw in the sky, Bharata, a radiance of a thousand suns."}},{"n":7,"text":"तस्य मध्यगतं चापि तेजसः पाण्डुनन्दन ।\nइन्द्रायुधपिनद्धाङ्गं विद्युन्मालागवाक्षकम् ।\nनीलशैलचयप्रख्यं बलाकाभूषितं घनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the middle of that radiance, son of Pandu, I saw a cloud-like form with its limbs wrapped in rainbows and lightning garlands for windows, like a heap of dark mountains, adorned with cranes."}},{"n":8,"text":"तमास्थितश्च भगवान्देव्या सह महाद्युतिः ।\nतपसा तेजसा कान्त्या दीप्तया सह भार्यया ॥","meaning":{"en":"The blessed, radiant god was seated in it with the goddess, shining with austerity, splendor and luster, together with his consort."}},{"n":9,"text":"रराज भगवांस्तत्र देव्या सह महेश्वरः ।\nसोमेन सहितः सूर्यो यथा मेघस्थितस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The blessed Maheshvara shone there with the goddess, like the sun with the moon in a cloud."}},{"n":10,"text":"संहृष्टरोमा कौन्तेय विस्मयोत्फुल्ललोचनः ।\nअपश्यं देवसंघानां गतिमार्तिहरं हरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With hair bristling and eyes wide with wonder, son of Kunti, I saw Hara, refuge of the hosts of gods and remover of distress."}},{"n":11,"text":"किरीटिनं गदिनं शूलपाणिं\nव्याघ्राजिनं जटिलं दण्डपाणिम् ।\nपिनाकिनं वज्रिणं तीक्ष्णदंष्ट्रं\nशुभाङ्गदं व्यालयज्ञोपवीतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He wore a crown and carried a mace and trident; he wore a tiger skin, matted locks and a staff, bore the Pinaka bow and a thunderbolt, had sharp fangs, fine armlets and a serpent for sacred thread."}},{"n":12,"text":"दिव्यां मालामुरसानेकवर्णां\nसमुद्वहन्तं गुल्फदेशावलम्बाम् ।\nचन्द्रं यथा परिविष्टं ससंध्यं\nवर्षात्यये तद्वदपश्यमेनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"On his chest he bore a divine garland of many colors hanging to his ankles; I saw him like the moon in its halo at dusk at the end of the rains."}},{"n":13,"text":"प्रमथानां गणैश्चैव समन्तात्परिवारितम् ।\nशरदीव सुदुष्प्रेक्ष्यं परिविष्टं दिवाकरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was surrounded on every side by the hosts of Pramathas, like the sun in autumn, hard to look at, in its circle of light."}},{"n":14,"text":"एकादश तथा चैनं रुद्राणां वृषवाहनम् ।\nअस्तुवन्नियतात्मानः कर्मभिः शुभकर्मिणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The eleven Rudras, self-controlled, praised him, the doer of good deeds, the bull-rider, by their works."}},{"n":15,"text":"आदित्या वसवः साध्या विश्वेदेवास्तथाश्विनौ ।\nविश्वाभिः स्तुतिभिर्देवं विश्वदेवं समस्तुवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Adityas, Vasus, Sadhyas, Vishvedevas and the Ashvins praised the god, the god of all, with every praise."}},{"n":16,"text":"शतक्रतुश्च भगवान्विष्णुश्चादितिनन्दनौ ।\nब्रह्मा रथन्तरं साम ईरयन्ति भवान्तिके ॥","meaning":{"en":"Indra of a hundred sacrifices and the blessed Vishnu, the two sons of Aditi, and Brahma chanted the Rathantara chant near Bhava."}},{"n":17,"text":"योगीश्वराः सुबहवो योगदं पितरं गुरुम् ।\nब्रह्मर्षयश्च ससुतास्तथा देवर्षयश्च वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"Many lords of yoga, and brahmin sages with their sons, and divine sages too, praised the father and teacher who grants yoga."}},{"n":18,"text":"पृथिवी चान्तरिक्षं च नक्षत्राणि ग्रहास्तथा ।\nमासार्धमासा ऋतवो रात्र्यः संवत्सराः क्षणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Earth, sky, constellations and planets, months, fortnights, seasons, nights, years and moments,"}},{"n":19,"text":"मुहूर्ताश्च निमेषाश्च तथैव युगपर्ययाः ।\nदिव्या राजन्नमस्यन्ति विद्याः सर्वा दिशस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"instants and winks, and the cycles of ages, O king, and all divine sciences and the directions bow to him."}},{"n":20,"text":"सनत्कुमारो वेदाश्च इतिहासास्तथैव च ।\nमरीचिरङ्गिरा अत्रिः पुलस्त्यः पुलहः क्रतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanatkumara, the Vedas, the Itihasas, Marichi, Angiras, Atri, Pulastya, Pulaha and Kratu,"}},{"n":21,"text":"मनवः सप्तसोमश्च अथर्वा सबृहस्पतिः ।\nभृगुर्दक्षः कश्यपश्च वसिष्ठः काश्य एव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"the seven Manus, Soma, Atharvan with Brihaspati, Bhrigu, Daksha, Kashyapa, Vasishtha and Kashya,"}},{"n":22,"text":"छन्दांसि दीक्षा यज्ञाश्च दक्षिणाः पावको हविः ।\nयज्ञोपगानि द्रव्याणि मूर्तिमन्ति युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"the meters, consecration, sacrifices, gifts, fire, the offering, and the materials used in sacrifice, in embodied form, Yudhishthira,"}},{"n":23,"text":"प्रजानां पतयः सर्वे सरितः पन्नगा नगाः ।\nदेवानां मातरः सर्वा देवपत्न्यः सकन्यकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"all the lords of creatures, rivers, serpents, mountains, all the mothers of the gods, the wives of the gods and the maidens,"}},{"n":24,"text":"सहस्राणि मुनीनां च अयुतान्यर्बुदानि च ।\nनमस्यन्ति प्रभुं शान्तं पर्वताः सागरा दिशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"thousands, tens of thousands and hundreds of millions of sages, and mountains, oceans and quarters bow to the peaceful lord."}},{"n":25,"text":"गन्धर्वाप्सरसश्चैव गीतवादित्रकोविदाः ।\nदिव्यतानेन गायन्तः स्तुवन्ति भवमद्भुतम् ।\nविद्याधरा दानवाश्च गुह्यका राक्षसास्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gandharvas and apsarases, skilled in song and instruments, sing with divine harmony and praise the wonderful Bhava, as do Vidyadharas, Danavas, Guhyakas and Rakshasas."}},{"n":26,"text":"सर्वाणि चैव भूतानि स्थावराणि चराणि च ।\nनमस्यन्ति महाराज वाङ्मनःकर्मभिर्विभुम् ।\nपुरस्ताद्विष्ठितः शर्वो ममासीत्त्रिदशेश्वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All beings, moving and unmoving, bow, great king, in word, thought and deed to the all-pervading lord. Shiva, lord of the gods, stood before me."}},{"n":27,"text":"पुरस्ताद्विष्ठितं दृष्ट्वा ममेशानं च भारत ।\nसप्रजापतिशक्रान्तं जगन्मामभ्युदैक्षत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Ishana standing before me, Bharata, the world, with the lords of creatures and Indra, looked on me."}},{"n":28,"text":"ईक्षितुं च महादेवं न मे शक्तिरभूत्तदा ।\nततो मामब्रवीद्देवः पश्य कृष्ण वदस्व च ॥","meaning":{"en":"I had no strength then to look at Mahadeva. Then the god said to me, \"Look, Krishna, and speak.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"शिरसा वन्दिते देवे देवी प्रीता उमाभवत् ।\nततोऽहमस्तुवं स्थाणुं स्तुतं ब्रह्मादिभिः सुरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When I bowed my head to the god, the goddess Uma was pleased. Then I praised Sthanu, who is praised by Brahma and the gods."}},{"n":30,"text":"नमोऽस्तु ते शाश्वत सर्वयोने\nब्रह्माधिपं त्वामृषयो वदन्ति ।\nतपश्च सत्त्वं च रजस्तमश्च\nत्वामेव सत्यं च वदन्ति सन्तः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Homage to you, eternal source of all! Sages call you the lord of Brahma; the wise call you austerity, goodness, passion and darkness, and truth itself.\""}},{"n":31,"text":"त्वं वै ब्रह्मा च रुद्रश्च वरुणोऽग्निर्मनुर्भवः ।\nधाता त्वष्टा विधाता च त्वं प्रभुः सर्वतोमुखः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You are Brahma, Rudra, Varuna, Agni, Manu and Bhava; you are Dhata, Tvashtri and Vidhata, and the lord facing every direction.\""}},{"n":32,"text":"त्वत्तो जातानि भूतानि स्थावराणि चराणि च ।\nत्वमादिः सर्वभूतानां संहारश्च त्वमेव हि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"From you are born beings, moving and unmoving; you are the origin of all beings, and you alone are their destruction.\""}},{"n":33,"text":"ये चेन्द्रियार्थाश्च मनश्च कृत्स्नं\nये वायवः सप्त तथैव चाग्निः ।\nये वा दिविस्था देवताश्चापि पुंसां\nतस्मात्परं त्वामृषयो वदन्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The objects of the senses, the whole mind, the seven winds, and fire, and the deities who dwell in heaven for men: sages say you are beyond all of these.\""}},{"n":34,"text":"वेदा यज्ञाश्च सोमश्च दक्षिणा पावको हविः ।\nयज्ञोपगं च यत्किंचिद्भगवांस्तदसंशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The Vedas, sacrifices, Soma, the gift, fire, the offering, and whatever belongs to sacrifice: the blessed one is all that, without doubt.\""}},{"n":35,"text":"इष्टं दत्तमधीतं च व्रतानि नियमाश्च ये ।\nह्रीः कीर्तिः श्रीर्द्युतिस्तुष्टिः सिद्धिश्चैव त्वदर्पणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"What is sacrificed, given and studied, and the vows and disciplines, modesty, fame, prosperity, radiance, contentment and success are all offered to you.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"कामः क्रोधो भयं लोभो मदः स्तम्भोऽथ मत्सरः ।\nआधयो व्याधयश्चैव भगवंस्तनयास्तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Desire, anger, fear, greed, pride, rigidity and envy, mental pains and bodily ills, lord, are your offspring.\""}},{"n":37,"text":"कृतिर्विकारः प्रलयः प्रधानं प्रभवोऽव्ययः ।\nमनसः परमा योनिः स्वभावश्चापि शाश्वतः ।\nअव्यक्तः पावन विभो सहस्रांशो हिरण्मयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Action, transformation, dissolution, primal nature, origin, the imperishable, the supreme source of mind, and eternal inherent nature; you are the unmanifest, the purifier, the lord, thousand-rayed and golden.\""}},{"n":38,"text":"आदिर्गुणानां सर्वेषां भवान्वै जीवनाश्रयः ।\nमहानात्मा मतिर्ब्रह्मा विश्वः शंभुः स्वयंभुवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You are the source of all the qualities and the support of life; you are the great self, intellect, Brahma, the universe, Shambhu and the self-existent.\""}},{"n":39,"text":"बुद्धिः प्रज्ञोपलब्धिश्च संवित्ख्यातिर्धृतिः स्मृतिः ।\nपर्यायवाचकैः शब्दैर्महानात्मा विभाव्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Understanding, wisdom, perception, awareness, renown, steadiness and memory: by these synonymous words you are conceived as the great self.\""}},{"n":40,"text":"त्वां बुद्ध्वा ब्राह्मणो विद्वान्न प्रमोहं निगच्छति ।\nहृदयं सर्वभूतानां क्षेत्रज्ञस्त्वमृषिष्टुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Knowing you, the learned brahmin is not confused; you are the heart of all beings, the knower of the field, praised by sages.\""}},{"n":41,"text":"सर्वतःपाणिपादस्त्वं सर्वतोक्षिशिरोमुखः ।\nसर्वतःश्रुतिमाँल्लोके सर्वमावृत्य तिष्ठसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You have hands and feet everywhere, eyes, heads and faces everywhere, and hearing everywhere; you stand in the world enveloping everything.\""}},{"n":42,"text":"फलं त्वमसि तिग्मांशो निमेषादिषु कर्मसु ।\nत्वं वै प्रभार्चिः पुरुषः सर्वस्य हृदि संस्थितः ।\nअणिमा लघिमा प्राप्तिरीशानो ज्योतिरव्ययः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You, sharp-rayed one, are the fruit in actions beginning with the wink of an eye; you are the person of radiant light seated in every heart; you are the power of becoming small and light, the power of attaining, the lord, the imperishable light.\""}},{"n":43,"text":"त्वयि बुद्धिर्मतिर्लोकाः प्रपन्नाः संश्रिताश्च ये ।\nध्यानिनो नित्ययोगाश्च सत्यसंधा जितेन्द्रियाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"In you rest the understanding, the mind and the worlds, and those who take refuge in you: the meditators, those ever in yoga, the truthful and the self-controlled.\""}},{"n":44,"text":"यस्त्वां ध्रुवं वेदयते गुहाशयं\nप्रभुं पुराणं पुरुषं विश्वरूपम् ।\nहिरण्मयं बुद्धिमतां परां गतिं\nस बुद्धिमान्बुद्धिमतीत्य तिष्ठति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"One who knows you as the steady, the dweller in the cave of the heart, the ancient lord, the person of every form, the golden, the supreme goal of the wise, that wise man stands beyond wisdom.\""}},{"n":45,"text":"विदित्वा सप्त सूक्ष्माणि षडङ्गं त्वां च मूर्तितः ।\nप्रधानविधियोगस्थस्त्वामेव विशते बुधः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Knowing the seven subtle things and you in your six-limbed form, a wise man established in the practice of primal nature enters you alone.\""}},{"n":46,"text":"एवमुक्ते मया पार्थ भवे चार्तिविनाशने ।\nचराचरं जगत्सर्वं सिंहनादमथाकरोत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When I had spoken thus, son of Pritha, to Bhava, the remover of distress, the whole moving and unmoving world raised a lion's roar."}},{"n":47,"text":"सविप्रसंघाश्च सुरासुराश्च\nनागाः पिशाचाः पितरो वयांसि ।\nरक्षोगणा भूतगणाश्च सर्वे\nमहर्षयश्चैव तथा प्रणेमुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The brahmin hosts, gods and demons, nagas, pishachas, ancestors, birds, hosts of rakshasas and spirits, and the great sages all bowed."}},{"n":48,"text":"मम मूर्ध्नि च दिव्यानां कुसुमानां सुगन्धिनाम् ।\nराशयो निपतन्ति स्म वायुश्च सुसुखो ववौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Heaps of fragrant divine flowers fell on my head, and a very pleasant wind blew."}},{"n":49,"text":"निरीक्ष्य भगवान्देवीमुमां मां च जगद्धितः ।\nशतक्रतुं चाभिवीक्ष्य स्वयं मामाह शंकरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Looking at the goddess Uma, at me, and at Indra, the blessed Shankara, who seeks the world's good, himself spoke to me."}},{"n":50,"text":"विद्मः कृष्ण परां भक्तिमस्मासु तव शत्रुहन् ।\nक्रियतामात्मनः श्रेयः प्रीतिर्हि परमा त्वयि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"We know your supreme devotion to us, slayer of foes, Krishna. Do what is good for yourself; I have the highest affection for you.\""}},{"n":51,"text":"वृणीष्वाष्टौ वरान्कृष्ण दातास्मि तव सत्तम ।\nब्रूहि यादवशार्दूल यानिच्छसि सुदुर्लभान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Choose eight boons, Krishna; I will give them, best of men. Tell me, tiger of the Yadavas, whatever very hard-to-obtain things you wish.\""}}]}]}